---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, withBase } from '../consts';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Contact"
  description="How to reach AI Audio Report: corrections, pricing updates, licensing changes and general enquiries."
>
  <h1 class="page-title">Contact</h1>
  <p class="lede">One address. It goes straight to the editor.</p>

  <p style="font-size:1.2rem"><a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a></p>

  <h2>Who runs this</h2>
  <p>
    AI Audio Report is run and edited by <strong>Arnau Gran i Romero</strong>, and mail to the
    address above reaches him. Articles he has checked line by line name him as reviewer at
    the top of the page, so you can tell which ones have had that pass and which have not.
  </p>

  <h2>Worth emailing about</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>A price that is wrong, or has changed.</strong> Tell us which page and what you see
    now. This is the single most useful thing anyone sends us, and it goes to the front of the
    queue.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Licence terms that have been rewritten.</strong> Vendors change these quietly and
    rarely announce it, so a heads-up is genuinely valuable.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>A broken link, or a page that reads badly.</strong> If something here feels padded,
    evasive or like it is avoiding the actual question, say so and point at the paragraph.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>A correction from a vendor.</strong> If you work for a company covered here and we
    have misread your terms, tell us and it gets fixed. We will not run your marketing copy in
    exchange, and coverage is not for sale at any price.
  </p>

  <h2>Not worth emailing about</h2>
  <p>
    Guest posts, paid links, sponsored reviews and link exchanges are all declined, so there is
    no need to send that one. We also cannot tell you whether your particular release is legally
    in the clear. The note on any licensing article explains why that is reporting rather than
    advice.
  </p>

  <p>
    The <a href={withBase('/privacy/')}>privacy policy</a> covers what happens to an email you
    send: it is read, it is replied to, and it is not added to any list, because there is no
    list.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
